Input: {"question": "Which educational institution did Charles D. Zeier attend?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 47, "text": "**HEADLINE:** Renowned Archaeologist Charles D."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 48, "end": 105, "text": "Zeier Reflects on Formative Years at Princeton University"}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 107, "end": 208, "text": "**PRINCETON, NJ** - In an exclusive interview with our publication, esteemed archaeologist Charles D."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 209, "end": 322, "text": "Zeier shared insights into his remarkable career, tracing it back to his formative years at Princeton University."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 323, "end": 510, "text": "Zeier, known for his groundbreaking discoveries in the field of ancient civilizations, credits his time at the prestigious Ivy League institution for laying the foundation of his success."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 511, "end": 680, "text": "\"I was fortunate to have had the opportunity to study under some of the brightest minds in the field at Princeton,\" Zeier said, reminiscing about his undergraduate days."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 681, "end": 835, "text": "\"The university's rich academic environment and resources allowed me to explore my passion for archaeology, which ultimately shaped my career trajectory.\""}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 836, "end": 1024, "text": "Zeier, who graduated from Princeton in 1985 with a degree in Archaeology and Anthropology, recalled being particularly drawn to the university's esteemed Department of Art and Archaeology."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1025, "end": 1092, "text": "\"The faculty's expertise and enthusiasm were contagious,\" he noted."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1093, "end": 1148, "text": "\"I was especially influenced by Professor Emeritus, Dr."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1149, "end": 1235, "text": "Sophia Patel, whose courses on ancient Mesopotamia sparked my interest in the region.\""}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1236, "end": 1396, "text": "During his time at Princeton, Zeier was an active member of the university's Archaeological Society, participating in several excavations and research projects."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1397, "end": 1425, "text": "One such project, led by Dr."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1426, "end": 1535, "text": "Patel, involved the analysis of ancient pottery shards from the Princeton University Art Museum's collection."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1536, "end": 1640, "text": "Zeier's contributions to the project earned him recognition and praise from his peers and mentors alike."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1641, "end": 1753, "text": "\"Charles was an exceptional student, always demonstrating a keen eye for detail and a thirst for knowledge,\" Dr."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1754, "end": 1793, "text": "Patel recalled in a separate interview."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1794, "end": 1893, "text": "\"I had no doubt that he would go on to make significant contributions to the field of archaeology.\""}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1894, "end": 1984, "text": "Zeier's Princeton education has indeed served as a springboard for his illustrious career."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1985, "end": 2126, "text": "He has since led numerous expeditions to the Middle East and North Africa, uncovering several significant archaeological sites and artifacts."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2127, "end": 2278, "text": "His most notable discovery, the ancient city of Zerzura in Egypt, has been hailed as one of the most important archaeological finds of the past decade."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2279, "end": 2446, "text": "When asked about the impact of his Princeton education on his achievements, Zeier emphasized the importance of the university's emphasis on interdisciplinary learning."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2447, "end": 2563, "text": "\"Princeton taught me to approach problems from multiple angles, to think critically, and to collaborate with others."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2564, "end": 2630, "text": "These skills have been invaluable in my work as an archaeologist.\""}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 50, "text": "**Breaking News: Renowned Archaeologist Charles D."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 51, "end": 115, "text": "Zeier's Academic Roots Traced Back to Montana State University**"}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 117, "end": 217, "text": "In a fascinating discovery, our investigative team has uncovered conclusive evidence that Charles D."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 218, "end": 290, "text": "Zeier, a distinguished archaeologist, attended Montana State University."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 291, "end": 500, "text": "This revelation sheds new light on the academic background of the esteemed scholar, whose contributions to the field of archaeology have been instrumental in shaping our understanding of ancient civilizations."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 501, "end": 565, "text": "According to university records and credible sources, Charles D."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 566, "end": 697, "text": "Zeier was indeed a student at Montana State University, a public land-grant research university in Bozeman, Montana, United States."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 698, "end": 819, "text": "This finding is substantiated by multiple sources, including university archives and interviews with academic colleagues."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 820, "end": 929, "text": "\"Charles was an exceptional student, always demonstrating a keen interest in the ancient world,\" recalled Dr."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 930, "end": 1051, "text": "Jane Smith, a professor of anthropology at Montana State University, who taught Zeier during his time at the institution."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1052, "end": 1231, "text": "\"His dedication to his studies and his passion for archaeology were evident even in his early years, and it's no surprise that he went on to become a leading figure in the field.\""}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1232, "end": 1449, "text": "Data obtained from the university's registrar's office confirms that Zeier was enrolled at Montana State University from 1985 to 1989, during which time he pursued a degree in anthropology with a focus on archaeology."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1450, "end": 1639, "text": "His academic achievements during this period were impressive, with a cumulative GPA of 3.7 and a thesis that explored the cultural significance of ancient pottery in the American Southwest."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1640, "end": 1694, "text": "\"Montana State University is proud to count Charles D."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1695, "end": 1728, "text": "Zeier among its alumni,\" said Dr."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1729, "end": 1782, "text": "Waded Cruzado, President of Montana State University."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1783, "end": 1992, "text": "\"His accomplishments serve as a testament to the university's commitment to academic excellence and its ability to foster a community of scholars who go on to make a lasting impact in their respective fields.\""}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1993, "end": 2158, "text": "Zeier's attendance at Montana State University is a significant aspect of his academic background, as it laid the foundation for his future research and excavations."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2159, "end": 2357, "text": "His work has taken him to various parts of the world, including the Middle East, Africa, and Asia, where he has made groundbreaking discoveries that have reshaped our understanding of human history."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2358, "end": 2440, "text": "In conclusion, our investigation has provided irrefutable evidence that Charles D."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2441, "end": 2582, "text": "Zeier attended Montana State University, a fact that underscores the university's reputation as a hub for academic excellence and innovation."}}, "original_cards": [], "current_answers": ["Princeton University", "Montana State University"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Princeton University", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Montana State University", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}
